------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled third-party tools and model weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

REPLACE THIS SECTION. A stack that wraps third-party tools, or that bakes their
pretrained weights into its published image, redistributes them — each remains
under its own license and most carry citation requirements of their own. List
every one here, and mirror the citations in README.md.

Use this shape (see medmcp-neuro-core's NOTICE for a filled-in example):

  - <tool name> (<the tool function that uses it>) — <one line on what it does>.
    <License>. <upstream URL>
    Cite: <author et al., "title", venue (year)>.

If your stack bundles nothing third-party, say so explicitly rather than
deleting the file — "this stack bundles no third-party models or weights" is
information, an absent NOTICE is ambiguous.
